<div class="page-head">
  <div>
    <div class="eyebrow">Draft · first word goes out with your next send after launch</div>
    <h1>Next game <span class="badge badge-amber">Draft</span></h1>
  </div>
  <div class="actions">
    <%= button_to "Launch game", account_publication_game_launch_path(publication_id: @publication.id, game_id: game.id),
          method: :post, class: "btn btn-primary btn-small",
          form: { data: { turbo_confirm: "Launch this game? The first word goes out with your next send." } } %>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>What launch does</h2>
  <p class="small muted">Launching starts the game on the order below. One word goes out with each
    send, and any word that hasn't gone out yet can still be swapped or reordered. Nothing happens
    between sends.</p>
  <p class="small muted">Games run continuously. When one ends, the next starts on its own, and you
    can always adjust it here beforehand. Prizes and the sponsor live on the Sponsors &amp; Prizes
    tab and apply to every game.</p>
</div>

<div style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
  <%= render "word_list", game: game %>
</div>
